# Open-chain first stage for AML-A311D-CC (Alta), G12B.
# Product is aml-a311d-cc_defconfig (vendor bl2_new.bin, AML_ENCRYPT=g12b).
# This defconfig is product + G12/SM1 first-stage geometry + the TPL->SPL->FIT
# chain (AHB TPL 0xFFFA1000 / 0xf000, DRAM SPL 0x08000000) + the open-TF-A
# DRAM-start secure layout.  Used by LBS aml-a311d-cc-libre.
# Formerly stacked: aml-a311d-cc_defconfig + spl-g12a.config
# + spl-g12b-pll.config + libre-secure-g12a.config + olddefconfig.
#
# Retargeted onto the SM1 Strategy A orchestrator (g12b-transfer-assessment.md
# Phase S): the G12B and G12A DDR blob sets are the same firmware, so Alta runs
# dram-g12a.c's dram_init() and takes only its board power sequence from
# spl-g12b.c via CONFIG_MESON_G12B_POWER_INIT.  CONFIG_MESON_G12_OPEN_PLL
# (Strategy B Phase 1: lock the PLL, print CNTL0, hang) is deliberately NOT set
# here -- it would relink dram-g12.c in place of the orchestrator.
#
# NOT YET MEASURED ON SILICON: spl-g12b.c has never executed.  This target is
# build-verified only; Phase B is what proves it boots.
#
